  <revision rev="2" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>62d71557569557db2fdf00f3b01dd1b8</srcmd5>
    <version>0.4.0</version>
    <time>1786461531</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Update to 0.4.0: adds a call-scoped Frame mechanism (new uncalled_for.frames module) and CallArgument(&quot;name&quot;), which lets a dependency factory receive a value from the outer function call - usable as a factory parameter default or as a keyword binding in Depends(factory, **bindings). New public API: CallArgument, CycleError, Frame, current_frame, frame_scope. Existing resolution paths are unchanged (bare Depends(f) keeps its cache key, _resolve_parameters keeps its signature). Also fixes five pyright errors, four pre-existing. Packaging: %check now runs the full upstream test suite (121 tests, green on python313 and python314) instead of a bare import smoke test, adding pytest/pytest-asyncio BuildRequires; upstream's coverage and per-test-timeout addopts are CI-only gates and are dropped. LICENSE is now packaged. No dependency or requires-python changes (pyproject.toml is unchanged from 0.3.2). Local build green on openSUSE_Tumbleweed/aarch64, rpmlint 0 errors 0 warnings 0 badness.</comment>
    <requestid>1370575</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
